commit_message:
add GoogleMediaImporter via newly factored out GoogleVideoInterface (#1231)

completes fork of GooglePhotosImporter into GoogleMediaImporter

this PR introduces GoogleMediaImporter by forking the GooglePhotosImporter and fundamentally only adding new video-logic to it by relying on the previously-merged prefactored Video interface. so you can see this particular PR as a few steps:

1. `cp photos/GooglePhotosImporter.java media/GoogleMediaImporter.java`
2. all the obvious renames (class rename, `s/PhotosContainer/MediaContainer/g`, etc.)
3. internally refactor some model-looping logic with generics/method-references
4. utilize previous cleanup to introduce newly available Video logic (as of prefactor in PR#1229)
5. leave trail of TODOs for ourselves, that @aksingh737 (of google photos team) and I agreed on when planning this work; For example, things like: we factored out (to avoid duplicate code living adrift) Video logic in PR#1229, but we didn't factor out Photos logic, so right now much of GooglePhotosImporter could *also* be deleted (if we factor out GoogleMediaImporter's logic to a common interface).

------

here's the above explanation, but in diff form. git doesn't have a way to track file "copy" so the diff looks deceptive, as these files were copied from their GooglePhotos counterparts. here's some more meaningful diffs...

